WEBVTT

00:56:57.981 --> 00:57:00.378
And we're figuring out how
to use that technology.

00:57:00.402 --> 00:57:03.329
I have basic faith in, again,
our ability to figure stuff out.

00:57:03.353 --> 00:57:06.378
We'll figure out how to use
technology so it doesn't destroy us.

00:57:06.402 --> 00:57:09.862
CA: So, pull the camera back
and look out at the country and the world.

00:57:09.886 --> 00:57:14.388
Where are you, David, on
the pessimism-optimism spectrum, and why?

00:57:14.412 --> 00:57:15.836
DB: I'm a long-term optimist.

00:57:15.860 --> 00:57:20.849
In the 1990s, I covered Europe
and that part of the world,

00:57:20.873 --> 00:57:22.749
and I covered a bunch of great events.

00:57:22.773 --> 00:57:26.655
I covered the fall of the Berlin Wall,
German reunification,

00:57:26.679 --> 00:57:30.786
the end of the Soviet Union, Mandela
coming out of prison in South Africa,